# Transitive dependency of caddy:2-alpine (the runtime image we use).
# Upstream Caddy has migrated its direct dependency to go-jose v4, but
# something still pulls v3.0.4 into the final binary. Tracking until
# Caddy releases an image with go-jose/v3 >= v3.0.5.
#
# Not exploitable in our deployment: hashpad serves static files only;
# the JOSE code path is not reached at runtime.
CVE-2026-34986

# Go stdlib 1.26.8 / golang.org/x/net 0.59.0 inside the caddy binary of caddy:2-alpine.
# The newest published caddy:2-alpine (2026-10-06) still ships them, so a base-image
# bump cannot fix this. These are denial-of-service issues (HTTP/2 SETTINGS flood,
# crafted Range headers, TLS ECH) that Caddy does expose; mitigated only by running
# behind the cluster ingress/load balancer. Remove once Caddy rebuilds with Go >= 1.26.9
# and x/net >= 0.60.0 (review by 2026-11-16).
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031
